          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "জলখাবার — jôlkhābār — \"breakfast; a light meal\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "হোটেলে জলখাবারে লুচি আর আলুর তরকারি ছিল। hoṭele jôlkhābāre luchi ār ālur tôrkāri chhilô. At the hotel there were luchis and potato curry for breakfast."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literally water-food: the small meal taken with a glass of water, morning or afternoon."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "জলখাবার (jôlkhābār) joins জল, \"water\", Sanskrit jala (Monier-Williams), to খাবার, \"food\", from খাওয়া, to eat (CDIAL 3865); the whole means a light meal, not food and water."
            }
          ]
        },
